---
import EditorialCase from './EditorialCase.astro';
import StoryChapter from './StoryChapter.astro';
import type { WorkEntry } from '../../data/work';
interface Props { work: WorkEntry }
const { work } = Astro.props;
const productLink = work.links?.find(link => link.url.startsWith('https://www.buzzvil.com/'));
const lessons = [
  { title: 'Access is not commitment.', body: 'Removing an entry step helped more people reach the mission. Advertiser’s target actions stayed essentially flat in that comparison.' },
  { title: 'More choice can add friction.', body: 'Mission Mode looked plausible, but all three campaign/platform slices recorded lower advertiser target actions per install.' },
  { title: 'Prove it, then give it room to grow.', body: 'My early design work helped establish the model. Mido took ownership of ongoing design as the product and its distribution strategy expanded.' }
];
---
<EditorialCase
  {work}
  headline={'Game UA.\nBeyond the\ninstall.'}
  intro="I helped turn rewarded advertising from a single paid action into a journey through a product. Game UA, our approach to bringing new players into games, was where I designed and helped prove that model."
  role="Hands-on product design across discovery, onboarding and return paths. I later handed ongoing design to Mido, moving into guidance and review."
  website={productLink && { label: 'Visit Game UA’s website', url: productLink.url }}
  coverNote="A mission-page concept with sample game content."
  {lessons}
>
  <figure slot="cover" class="game-cover">
    <img src="/blog/i-dont-like-ads/ua.png" width="1178" height="1230" alt="Two illustrative mission-page screens connecting a game introduction to rewarded in-game progress" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" />
  </figure>

  <game-ua-case>
    <StoryChapter id="game-ua-questions" scope="The product idea" title={'From paying for an action\nto designing what happens next.'} intro="In a cost-per-action campaign, or CPA, the advertiser pays when someone completes a defined action. The campaigns we wanted to move beyond centered on that single moment. But an install alone did not mean someone had discovered the game or found a reason to keep playing.">
      <figure class="campaign-model">
        <div class="model-before"><span class="model-label">The starting point</span><h3>One action.<br/>One reward.</h3><div class="single-action"><span>Install the game</span><strong>Reward</strong></div><p>The campaign reached its goal. What happened inside the game remained the harder question.</p></div>
        <div class="model-after"><span class="model-label">The shift we designed</span><h3>A sequence of steps<br/>inside the experience.</h3><ol class="model-steps"><li><span>01</span><strong>Get started</strong><p>Enter the game.</p><small>Reward</small></li><li><span>02</span><strong>Discover it</strong><p>Reach a first milestone.</p><small>Reward</small></li><li><span>03</span><strong>Go further</strong><p>Progress toward the next goal.</p><small>Reward</small></li></ol></div>
        <figcaption>The campaign model, illustrated.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="model-meaning"><h3>The campaign became<br/>part of the product journey.</h3><p>We connected rewards to steps inside the game. Players could see what to do next and what they would earn; advertisers could guide participation beyond the initial install. My early design work made that sequence understandable and helped establish that the model was worth developing.</p></div>
    </StoryChapter>

    <StoryChapter id="game-ua-pattern" scope="Beyond games" title={'The reusable idea was the journey,\nnot the game.'} intro="We then separated this approach from the game-specific experience and carried it into brand and shopping experiences. The content could change; the underlying idea stayed the same: help someone discover a product through a sequence of clear, rewarded steps.">
      <div class="journey-applications" aria-label="How the same approach extends across product experiences">
        <article><span>Games</span><h3>From install<br/>to participation.</h3><p>Introduce the game, make progress visible and give the player a next goal.</p></article>
        <article><span>Brands</span><h3>From seeing a campaign<br/>to discovering a product.</h3><p>Give people an experience with the brand, beyond a view or a click.</p></article>
        <article><span>Shopping</span><h3>From browsing<br/>toward a purchase.</h3><p>Organize the experience around steps that bring someone closer to the advertiser’s goal.</p></article>
      </div>
      <p class="model-boundary">These describe the design approach across experiences, not a claim that every journey led to a purchase.</p>
      <a class="pattern-link" href="/work/interaction-composer/">Explore the later research into personalized brand experiences</a>
      <div class="study-bridge"><h3>A larger idea.<br/>Specific problems to solve.</h3><p>A sequence can also create friction. Could people get into it easily? Did choosing their rewards help? Did they understand and trust their progress? The following studies examine those questions, across my early work and the team’s later experiments.</p></div>
    </StoryChapter>
    <StoryChapter id="entry" scope="Zoom in · Getting into the mission" class="case-scene entry-scene" title={'Removing a screen\nmade the first step easier.'} intro="The explanation page repeated information already on the mission page. I proposed going straight to the experience, with a campaign switch to make the change reversible.">
      <figure class="entry-board">
        <div class="board-top"><span>Web UA / entry journey</span><div class="view-switch" role="group" aria-label="Compare the Web UA entry path"><button type="button" data-entry="before" aria-pressed="true">Before</button><button type="button" data-entry="direct" aria-pressed="false">Remove the bridge</button></div></div>
        <div class="entry-journey" data-entry-state="before">
          <div class="journey-node ad-node"><div class="mini-ad" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><i></i><i></i><b></b></div><span>Ad</span></div>
          <span class="journey-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="journey-node bridge-node"><div class="mini-bridge" aria-hidden="true"><b></b><i></i><i></i><i></i><span></span></div><span>Explanation</span></div>
          <span class="journey-line second-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="journey-node mission-node"><div class="mini-mission" aria-hidden="true"><div><b></b><i></i></div><span><i></i><b></b></span><span><i></i><b></b></span><span><i></i><b></b></span></div><span>Mission</span></div>
        </div>
        <p class="journey-summary" data-entry-caption aria-live="polite">One more explanation before the player could begin.</p>
        <div class="entry-results">
          <div class="result-pair"><h3>Reached the mission</h3><div><span><b>35%</b>Before</span><span><b>67%</b>After</span></div><p>People reaching the mission page<br/>as a share of people clicking the ad</p></div>
          <div class="result-pair"><h3>Installed the game</h3><div><span><b>7.8%</b>Before</span><span><b>10.4%</b>After</span></div><p>People installing the game<br/>as a share of people clicking the ad</p></div>
          <div class="entry-finding"><span>Advertiser’s target actions</span><strong>Essentially flat.</strong><p>Easier entry left the harder question inside the experience.</p></div>
        </div>
        <figcaption>A banking partner’s app, 2024. Before/after comparison; other campaign changes may have affected the result. Journey illustrated.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </StoryChapter>

    <StoryChapter id="choice" scope="Zoom in · Choosing a reward structure" class="case-scene" title={'Choosing a reward path\ndid not improve conversion.'} intro="Getting people into the mission did not guarantee meaningful play. In a separate experiment, a feature called Mission Mode tested whether choosing a reward structure would build commitment. The first option dominated; few people explored the alternatives.">
      <div class="choice-study">
        <figure class="choice-phones">
          <a href="/work/game-ua/mission-mode-choice.webp" aria-label="Open the original Mission Mode choice design"><img src="/work/game-ua/mission-mode-choice.webp" width="383" height="820" alt="Original Mission Mode design asking the player to choose a reward style in a horizontal carousel" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="/work/game-ua/mission-mode-confirm.webp" aria-label="Open the original Mission Mode confirmation design"><img src="/work/game-ua/mission-mode-confirm.webp" width="383" height="820" alt="Original confirmation screen listing the selected missions and warning that the choice cannot be changed" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a>
          <figcaption>Original designs: choose a reward structure, then confirm it. Sample missions and rewards.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <div class="choice-finding">
          <h3>The test did not support<br/>adding that decision.</h3>
          <div class="comparison-chart" aria-label="One Android campaign: control 52.18 percent, Mission Mode 40.59 percent advertiser events per install">
            <div><span>Control <b>52.18%</b></span><i style="--bar:52.18%"></i><small>824 events / 1,579 installs</small></div>
            <div><span>Mission Mode <b>40.59%</b></span><i style="--bar:40.59%"></i><small>772 events / 1,902 installs</small></div>
          </div>
          <p class="figure-note">One Android campaign, 2025: target actions per install. Results are directional; test assignment is unconfirmed.</p>
          <p>All three campaign/platform slices declined on this measure. Some purchase counts moved the other way. The result called for investigation, not a success claim.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </StoryChapter>

    <StoryChapter id="return" scope="Zoom in · Trust and reasons to return" class="case-scene" title={'Progress needed a goal.\nRewards needed trust.'} intro="The early feedback study exposed uncertainty about rewards. Later, the team tested a different part of engagement: giving people a nearby goal to pursue.">
      <div class="return-study">
        <figure class="ranking-phone"><a href="/work/game-ua/ranking-board.webp" aria-label="Open the original Ranking Board design"><img src="/work/game-ua/ranking-board.webp" width="383" height="820" alt="Original Ranking Board design showing nearby ranks, a next-rank prompt and an attendance entry" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a><figcaption>The team’s later ranking-board design, shown with sample values.</figcaption></figure>
        <div class="return-evidence">
          <div class="feedback-findings">
            <div class="findings-heading"><h3>What the comments exposed</h3><span>September 2024</span></div>
            <div class="feedback-counts"><p><strong>1,472</strong> ratings</p><p><strong>277</strong> written comments</p></div>
            <ul class="feedback-themes" aria-label="Themes from user feedback"><li><i aria-hidden="true"></i>Missing rewards</li><li><i aria-hidden="true"></i>Delayed rewards</li><li><i aria-hidden="true"></i>Unclear payout timing</li></ul>
            <p class="figure-note">Themes from player feedback, 2024.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="ranking-findings">
            <div class="findings-heading"><h3>More visitors opened the game experience</h3><span>January–February 2026</span></div>
            <div class="ranking-results"><span><b>8%</b>Without the board</span><span><b>24%</b>With the board</span></div>
            <p class="figure-note">Share of daily visitors opening the game-rewards experience. Team comparison, 2026; rounded figures. Group sizes and test assignment remain unconfirmed.</p>
            <p>More people opened RewardMon. That finding does not establish longer sessions, repeat visits or revenue growth.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </StoryChapter>

    <StoryChapter id="scale" scope="Back to the product · Reach and investment" class="case-scene" title={'Growth exposed the limits\nof partner inventory.'} intro="The early product work helped make the case for greater investment in 2025. By 2026, the strategy had to address a new constraint: how many more players the existing placements could reach.">
      <div class="growth-board">
        <figure class="revenue-figure">
          <h3>Game UA revenue</h3>
          <div class="revenue-chart">
            <div class="revenue-row"><span>2024</span><div><i style="--bar:15.76%"></i></div><strong>₩788M</strong></div>
            <div class="revenue-row"><span>2025</span><div><i style="--bar:64.18%"></i></div><strong>₩3.209B</strong></div>
            <p>2025 target <b>₩5B</b></p>
          </div>
          <figcaption>Revenue grew about fourfold, but fell short of the ₩5B target. A shared product, sales and engineering outcome.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <div class="distribution-pivot">
          <h3>The reachable audience was narrowing.</h3>
          <div class="audience-comparison"><div><strong>~42k</strong><span>H1 2025</span></div><span class="audience-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span><div><strong>~32k</strong><span>H2 2025</span></div></div>
          <p class="figure-note">Average monthly new users. The team saw the decline as a sign that existing partner placements were reaching their limit.</p>
          <div class="strategy-routes"><span>Reaching previous visitors</span><span>Referrals</span><span>Standalone service</span></div>
          <p>The 2026 strategy widened the journey beyond partner placements. These were directions to develop: the first-half review said external retargeting had not progressed as intended.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </StoryChapter>

    <StoryChapter id="handoff" class="case-scene handoff-scene" title={'Mido, our designer, took over.\nMy focus moved to new systems.'} intro="I handed ongoing design to Mido: mission hierarchy, progress and rewards, retention experiments and the standalone experience. My role moved toward guidance and review.">
      <figure class="handoff-build">
        <div class="build-media">
          <div class="recorded-phone"><video controls playsinline preload="none" poster="/work/game-ua/hub.webp" width="572" height="1250" aria-label="July 2026 QA recording of the Game UA hub and genre-selection journey"><source src="/work/game-ua/hub-discovery.mp4" type="video/mp4"/><a href="/work/game-ua/hub-discovery.mp4">Watch the recorded build</a></video></div>
          <div class="discovery-phone"><img src="/work/game-ua/discovery.webp" width="572" height="1250" alt="The recorded QA build's genre picker, offering six game categories and up to three choices" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></div>
        </div>
        <figcaption>The team’s later test build: rewards and genre selection lead into game discovery.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="handoff-close"><p>My focus shifted to Buzzvil’s AI-native organization and web readiness ahead of a planned stock-market listing. The next design problem was helping more people move from intent to implementation, with a clear way to review what ships.</p><a href="/work/buzzvil-mediums/">Continue with Buzzvil mediums</a></div>
    </StoryChapter>
  </game-ua-case>
</EditorialCase>

<script>
class GameUACase extends HTMLElement {
  connectedCallback() {
    if (this.dataset.ready) return;
    this.dataset.ready = 'true';
    const journey = this.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-entry-state]');
    const caption = this.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-entry-caption]');
    this.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-entry]').forEach(button => {
      button.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const direct = button.dataset.entry === 'direct';
        if (journey) journey.dataset.entryState = direct ? 'direct' : 'before';
        this.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-entry]').forEach(control => control.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(control === button)));
        if (caption) caption.textContent = direct ? 'Straight to the mission. The information was already there.' : 'One more explanation before the player could begin.';
      });
    });
  }
}
if (!customElements.get('game-ua-case')) customElements.define('game-ua-case', GameUACase);
</script>

<style>
.campaign-model { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .8fr 1.3fr; border: 1px solid var(--theme-border); }
.model-before,.model-after { padding: clamp(1.25rem,3vw,2.75rem); min-width: 0; }
.model-after { background: var(--case-soft); border-left: 1px solid var(--theme-border); }
.model-label { font: .75rem/1.5 var(--font-mono); color: var(--theme-text-muted); }
.campaign-model h3 { font: 400 clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2.4rem)/1.2 var(--font-heading); margin: 1rem 0 2rem; letter-spacing: -.035em; }
.single-action { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; border-block: 1px solid var(--theme-border); padding: 1.5rem 0; font: .9rem/1.5 var(--font-body); }
.single-action strong,.model-steps small { font: .7rem/1.5 var(--font-mono); padding: .4rem .65rem; border: 1px solid var(--theme-border); border-radius: 20px; font-weight: 400; }
.model-before>p { color: var(--theme-text-muted); margin-top: 1.5rem; }
.model-steps { list-style: none; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr)); padding: 0; margin: 0; gap: 1.25rem; }
.model-steps li { border-top: 2px solid var(--theme-accent); padding-top: 1rem; }
.model-steps li>span { display: block; font: .7rem/1.5 var(--font-mono); color: var(--theme-text-muted); margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
.model-steps strong { font: 500 1rem/1.4 var(--font-body); }
.model-steps p { margin: .75rem 0 1.25rem; font-size: .85rem; color: var(--theme-text-muted); }
.model-steps small { display: inline-block; }
.campaign-model>figcaption { grid-column: 1/-1; padding: 1rem 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--theme-border); font: .75rem/1.6 var(--font-body); color: var(--theme-text-muted); }
.model-meaning,.study-bridge { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.4fr; gap: 2rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; }
.model-meaning h3,.study-bridge h3 { font: 400 clamp(1.4rem,2.5vw,2rem)/1.3 var(--font-heading); }
.model-meaning p,.study-bridge p { color: var(--theme-text-muted); }
.journey-applications { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 2rem; }
.journey-applications article { border-top: 2px solid var(--theme-border); padding-top: 1.25rem; }
.journey-applications article>span { font: .75rem/1.5 var(--font-mono); color: var(--theme-text-muted); }
.journey-applications h3 { margin: 1.2rem 0; font: 400 clamp(1.3rem,2.3vw,1.8rem)/1.3 var(--font-heading); }
.journey-applications p { color: var(--theme-text-muted); }
.model-boundary { margin: 1.5rem 0 .75rem; font-size: .75rem; color: var(--theme-text-muted); }
.pattern-link { font: .85rem/1.6 var(--font-body); text-decoration: underline; }
.study-bridge { border-top: 1px solid var(--theme-border); padding-top: 2rem; margin-top: 3rem; }
@media(max-width:700px) { .campaign-model { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .model-after { border-left: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--theme-border); } .model-meaning,.study-bridge { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1rem; } .journey-applications { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.75rem; } .model-steps { gap: .75rem; } .model-steps strong { font-size: .85rem; } .model-steps p { font-size: .75rem; } }

.game-cover { margin:0; background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--theme-text) 4%,var(--theme-bg)); padding:clamp(1.25rem,4vw,3rem); display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:2rem; overflow:hidden; }
.game-cover img { display:block; width:100%; max-width:690px; height:auto; margin:auto; }
game-ua-case { --case-soft:color-mix(in srgb,var(--theme-text) 4%,var(--theme-bg)); --case-shape:color-mix(in srgb,var(--theme-text) 16%,var(--theme-bg)); display:block; color:var(--theme-text); }
game-ua-case *, .game-cover * { box-sizing:border-box; }
h3,p,figure { margin:0; }
h3 { font:400 1.05rem/1.45 var(--font-mono,monospace); letter-spacing:-.025em; }
p { font:.94rem/1.8 var(--font-body,sans-serif); }
a { color:inherit; text-underline-offset:5px; text-decoration-color:var(--theme-border); }
a:hover { text-decoration-color:currentColor; }
a:focus-visible,button:focus-visible { outline:2px solid var(--theme-text); outline-offset:5px; }
figcaption,.figure-note { font:.78rem/1.75 var(--font-mono,monospace); color:var(--theme-text-muted); }
figcaption { margin-top:1rem; }
.entry-board { border:1px solid var(--theme-border); padding:clamp(1rem,3vw,2rem); }
.board-top { display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; gap:1rem; }
.board-top>span { font:.75rem/1.6 var(--font-mono,monospace); color:var(--theme-text-muted); }
.view-switch { display:flex; gap:.35rem; }
.view-switch button { font:.78rem/1.5 var(--font-mono,monospace); color:var(--theme-text); min-height:44px; padding:.65rem .8rem; border:1px solid var(--theme-border); background:var(--theme-bg); cursor:pointer; }
.view-switch button[aria-pressed=true] { background:var(--theme-text); color:var(--theme-bg); border-color:var(--theme-text); }
.entry-journey { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr .5fr 1fr .5fr 1fr; gap:1rem; align-items:center; max-width:650px; margin:3rem auto 1.5rem; }
.journey-node { min-width:0; display:flex; flex-direction:column; align-items:center; gap:1rem; }
.journey-node>span { font:.7rem/1.5 var(--font-mono,monospace); }
.journey-line { height:1px; background:var(--theme-border); margin-bottom:2.5rem; }
.mini-ad,.mini-bridge,.mini-mission { width:100%; max-width:140px; height:180px; border:1px solid var(--theme-border); padding:14px; background:var(--theme-bg); border-radius:8px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:10px; }
.mini-ad>span { display:block; height:72px; background:var(--case-shape); border-radius:4px; }
.mini-ad>i,.mini-bridge>i { height:4px; background:var(--case-shape); width:85%; }
.mini-ad>i:nth-of-type(2),.mini-bridge>i:nth-of-type(2) { width:55%; }
.mini-ad>b,.mini-bridge>span { height:20px; background:var(--theme-text); margin-top:auto; border-radius:3px; }
.mini-bridge>b { height:30px; background:var(--case-shape); width:45%; margin:12px 0; }
.mini-mission>div { display:flex; gap:8px; align-items:center; height:40px; }
.mini-mission>div>b { width:35px; height:35px; background:var(--case-shape); border-radius:5px; }
.mini-mission>div>i { width:45%; height:5px; background:var(--case-shape); }
.mini-mission>span { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:9px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--theme-border); padding:8px 0; }
.mini-mission>span>i { width:11px; height:11px; border:1px solid var(--theme-text-muted); border-radius:50%; }
.mini-mission>span>b { width:65%; height:4px; background:var(--case-shape); }
.bridge-node { transition:opacity .4s,transform .4s; }
.entry-journey[data-entry-state=direct] .bridge-node { opacity:.16; transform:scale(.88); }
.entry-journey[data-entry-state=direct] .bridge-node .mini-bridge { background:repeating-linear-gradient(-45deg,transparent 0,transparent 8px,var(--case-soft) 8px,var(--case-soft) 9px); }
.entry-journey[data-entry-state=direct] .journey-line { background:var(--theme-text); }
.journey-summary { text-align:center; font:.8rem/1.7 var(--font-mono,monospace); min-height:2.7rem; }
.entry-results { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1.15fr; gap:1.75rem; margin-top:2rem; padding-top:1.75rem; border-top:1px solid var(--theme-border); }
.result-pair h3 { font-size:.75rem; }
.result-pair>div { display:flex; gap:1.5rem; margin:.9rem 0; }
.result-pair>div>span { font:.75rem/1.7 var(--font-mono,monospace); color:var(--theme-text-muted); }
.result-pair b { display:block; color:var(--theme-text); font-weight:400; font-size:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem); letter-spacing:-.06em; }
.result-pair p { font:.75rem/1.7 var(--font-mono,monospace); color:var(--theme-text-muted); }
.entry-finding { border-left:1px solid var(--theme-border); padding-left:1.75rem; }
.entry-finding>span { font:.75rem/1.6 var(--font-mono,monospace); color:var(--theme-text-muted); }
.entry-finding strong { display:block; font:400 1.35rem/1.3 var(--font-mono,monospace); letter-spacing:-.04em; margin:.7rem 0; }
.entry-finding p { font-size:.8rem; }
.choice-study { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1.45fr 1fr; gap:clamp(1.5rem,4vw,3rem); align-items:center; }
.choice-phones { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:1rem; padding:clamp(1rem,3vw,2rem); background:var(--case-soft); }
.choice-phones a { display:block; }
.choice-phones img,.ranking-phone img { display:block; width:100%; height:auto; }
.choice-phones figcaption { grid-column:1/-1; margin-top:0; }
.choice-finding>h3 { font-size:1.35rem; letter-spacing:-.04em; }
.comparison-chart { margin:2rem 0 1rem; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:1.25rem; }
.comparison-chart>div>span { display:flex; justify-content:space-between; gap:1rem; font:.7rem/1.5 var(--font-mono,monospace); }
.comparison-chart b { font-weight:400; }
.comparison-chart i { display:block; position:relative; height:8px; background:var(--case-soft); margin:.65rem 0 .4rem; }
.comparison-chart i:after { content:''; display:block; width:var(--bar); height:100%; background:var(--theme-accent); }
